<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Danish Wise Men see 97 budget surplus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Danish Wise Men see 97 budget surplus.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The independent Danish Economic Council said in its biannual report on Wednesday that it expected a 1997 public sector budget surplus of 5.3 billion crowns, rising to 6.8 billion crowns in 1998.</p>
<p>In its previous report last November, the council, known as the Wise Men, forecast a public sector budget deficit of 4.1 billion crowns in 1997.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969650</p>
